@X0EPCBoard 15.3 contains some new listserver functionality.  This function allows
you to send a particular message to any number of addresses, which are
contained in a list (file), and save your message only once.  This means you
do not need to enter the addresses when entering the message, and you do not
end up with a message for each using being posted in the message base.  This
document will walk SysOps through the setup and operation of the listserver
function.
 
@X0BSETTING UP A LIST
-----------------
 
@X03There are 4 steps to setting up a list.
 
@X02STEP 1 - NAMES LIST
-------------------
@X03
First, create a file by any name and put it anywhere on your network.  In this
file are the names to send a message to.  Ex.
 
@X07phil.gilmore@saltair.com
cory.robin@saltair.com
askjay@aol.com
jmartin@xmission.com
 
@X03with one name on each line, beginning on line 1.  This is your names list.  You
can edit this file at any time without changing any other setup parameters.
 
@X02STEP 2 - ALIAS.OUT FILE
-----------------------
 
@X03Next, you must make an entry in your ALIAS.OUT file.  The location of your
ALIAS.OUT file is specified in PCBSetup.  Edit this file and append a line to
the end of it.  This line should indicate a BBS name, and then an alias.  The
Alias should be the name of the list, preceded by a % character.  Ex.
 
bbs.user,%c:\pcb\uucp\employees
 
Would indicate that the user on your BBS is named BBS USER.  This is not an
actual user, but simply the name in the FROM field of the message to send.
 
@X02STEP 3 - CREATE A USER RECORD
-----------------------------
 
@X03You must have a user record for each list that you use.  The user record needs
to have a user name which is entered in the ALIAS.OUT file before the
specification of the list filename.
 
You'll want to make sure the user is registered in the e-mail conference and
has sufficient security to enter a message in that conference.  Make sure that
the password is something that nobody can guess.  This account could still be
used to gain access to your BBS.
 
@X02

@X0BOPERATION
---------
 
@X02STEP 4 - ENTERING THE MESSAGE
-----------------------------
@X03
Enter the message to the sysop.  The body of the message can be anything you
would put in a normal e-mail message.  When you're finished, edit the message
header.  Change the from field to your LISTSERVER user name.  Save the message.
You'll only see the one message in the message base.  Now do a mail run.  You
will see UUXFER send that message to each user in the list.



















 
